    context: "The Bible shows God calling leaders in different ways. Moses met God at a burning bush and protested his inadequacy. Isaiah saw the Lord in the temple, confessed his uncleanness and was cleansed before being commissioned. In the New Testament, Paul told Timothy that desiring to be an overseer is a good desire. The writer of Hebrews insists that ministry is not taken by self-appointment. At Antioch, the Holy Spirit spoke to a praying and fasting church, which laid hands on Barnabas and Saul and sent them. Calling involves God, the individual and the church.",
